From: Trista Hsiao <trista_hsiao@accton.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ip_tunnel_core: check in_dev before netif_is_vxlan

iptunnel_xmit() looks up the input interface only when skb_iif is set
and then calls netif_is_vxlan(in_dev), which dereferences in_dev. A
packet the device sends itself has no input interface, so in_dev is
NULL and the kernel oopses; a WireGuard handshake sent by wg0 hits it.

Check in_dev first, as the qca-wifi-7 kernels already do (QCA change
Ia1d38441bf37af691d2afab7f5545a721192e83e).

--- a/net/ipv4/ip_tunnel_core.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/ip_tunnel_core.c
@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@
 		in_dev = __dev_get_by_index(&init_net, skb_iif);
 	}
 
-	if (proto == IPPROTO_IPV6 || proto == IPPROTO_GRE || netif_is_vxlan(in_dev)) {
+	if (proto == IPPROTO_IPV6 || proto == IPPROTO_GRE || (in_dev && netif_is_vxlan(in_dev))) {
 		skb->skb_iif = skb_iif;
 	}
 
